    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Past of być",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **być** («to be») has different past forms depending on the person: **byłem** («I was», man), **byłam** («I was», woman), **byłeś/byłaś** («you were»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Gender in the past",
     "texto": [
      "In the singular, the form also shows the gender of the person speaking or the person spoken about.",
      "Polish usually drops the pronoun when it is already clear who is meant."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
